      <h1 id="configuring-registry-storage-vsphere" class="group scroll-mt-20">Configuring the registry for vSphere<a href="#configuring-registry-storage-vsphere" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p>Configure image registry storage for vSphere clusters after installation. Because vSphere installations do not automatically provision storage, you must change the registry management state from <code>Removed</code> to <code>Managed</code> and configure persistent storage or use Red Hat OpenShift Data Foundation before the registry can store container images.</p>
